TrustPolicyDocument.description_cn:
角色信任策略。信任策略遵循IAM的[策略语法](https://www.volcengine.com/docs/6257/65059)中基于资源的策略规则。
- 以下是角色信任账号2000000001的信任策略示例：
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRole"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "IAM": [
				          "trn:iam::2000000001:root"
			          ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```
- 以下是角色信任ecs服务的信任策略示例：
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRole"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "Service": [
                    "ecs"
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```
注意：SSO场景使用AssumeRoleWithOIDC或AssumeRoleWithSAML接口进行角色扮演访问，因此角色信任策略中的Action部分需要替换成实际请求的接口，例如以下是一个用户SAML SSO的角色信任策略示例：
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "Federated": [
                    "trn:iam::2000000001:saml-provider/your-idp"
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

TrustPolicyDocument.description_en:
Role trust policy. Trust policies follow the resource-based policy rules defined in the IAM [policy syntax](https://www.volcengine.com/docs/6257/65059).
- The following is an example of a trust policy for a role that trusts account 2000000001:
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRole"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "IAM": [
                    "trn:iam::2000000001:root"
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```
- The following is an example of a trust policy for a role that trusts the ecs service:
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRole"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "Service": [
                    "ecs"
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```
Note: In SSO scenarios, the AssumeRoleWithOIDC or AssumeRoleWithSAML API is used to assume the role. Therefore, you need to replace the Action field in the trust policy with the actual API being called. For example, here is a sample trust policy for a user SAML SSO scenario:
```json
{
    "Statement": [
        {
            "Effect": "Allow",
            "Action": [
                "sts:AssumeRoleWithSAML"
            ],
            "Principal": {
                "Federated": [
                    "trn:iam::2000000001:saml-provider/your-idp"
                ]
            }
        }
    ]
}
```

